# The Tomb of Aclazotz (CR 601.3, 118.9, 601.2b): its way is a permission, not an alternative cost, so the Dracogenesis another permanent gives ("cast Dragon spells
# without paying their mana costs") may be used for the creature it lets Bot1 cast from the graveyard. Dracogenesis comes first (turn 3: Show and Tell, paid with Black Lotus, puts it onto
# the battlefield); the Journal is turned over on turn 5 and its hand - the Phyrexian Dragon Engine, a Lightning Bolt and a Plains - falls into the graveyard. On turn 7 the Tomb
# gives the way: the Engine is cast for nothing and is a Vampire as well, and the Bolt - no creature - is not offered, though it has a mana cost.

[Bot1 Deck]
Tarrian's Journal
Show and Tell
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Phyrexian Dragon Engine
Dracogenesis
Lightning Bolt
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Tarrian's Journal.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Dracogenesis)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Tarrian's Journal.Activate(Ability: Transform)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.The Tomb of Aclazotz.Activate(Ability: You may cast)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Graveyard.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Ability: You may cast)
Bot1.Graveyard.Phyrexian Dragon Engine.Cast(Ability: Without paying)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Phyrexian Dragon Engine.Subtypes = Dragon; Phyrexian; Vampire
Bot1.Battlefield.Phyrexian Dragon Engine.Counters.Finality = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Tapped = false
Bot1.Graveyard = Plains; Lightning Bolt; Show and Tell; Black Lotus
